# Byte-identical checkouts on every platform.
#
# The SHA-256 values in each benchmark's checksums_sha256.txt are computed over the bytes
# stored in this repository. Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true, which
# rewrites line endings on checkout; a reviewer cloning there would then fail every
# checksum in the package while nothing was actually wrong with the data. Turning text
# conversion off for everything keeps a clone byte-for-byte identical to what was
# published, which is the only state in which those checksums mean anything.
* -text
